react-standards: This project follows a modular architecture with the following structure:
- /src
  - /common (shared assets, components, hooks, layouts, lib, providers, services, stores, types, utils)
  - /features (feature-specific modules)
    - shared assets, components, hooks, layouts, lib, providers, services, stores, types, utils
  - /views (page-level components that compose UI from components)
    - Each view corresponds to a specific route
    - Views import and compose components from /common and /features
    - Views handle page-level state and logic
  - /routes (router configuration)
    - Routes import views from /views folder
    - Handles route definitions and configurations
  - App.tsx
  - main.tsx
  
Standards:
1. Abstract third-party services behind service interfaces
2. Use feature-based folders for domain-specific code
3. Keep components atomic and reusable
4. Use TanStack Router with type-safe routes
5. Follow shadcn/ui component patterns
6. Use Zustand for global state management 
7. Views should focus on composition and layout, not complex logic
8. Views connect components to data sources and services 